ees\nParents and Families\nAlumni and Friends\nCommunity and Business\nProspective Employees\nInfo For\nBlackboard\nEmail\nMicrosoft 365\nMyNIU\nAnywhere Apps\nHuskie Hub\nHuskies Get Hired\nMyScholarships\nNavigate\nPassword Reset / AccountID Lookup\nQualtrics\nQuick Links\nThe Graduate School\nAcademic Programs\nDoctoral Degree Programs\nDoctoral Degree Programs\nEarning a doctoral degree is the highest level of academic achievement, and NIU's doctoral programs are designed to take you there. Whether you're pursuing a Ph.D., Ed.D., Au.D., D.P.T. or D.N.P., you'll gain expert-level knowledge, advanced research skills and the credentials to lead in your field.\nDoctoral study typically combines specialized coursework, seminars and research-intensive training with a dissertation or thesis \u2014 an original research project completed under the guidance of a faculty advisor that contributes new knowledge to your discipline. Some programs also include teaching or practicum requirements.\nA doctoral degree opens doors well beyond academia. Graduates pursue careers in research, administration, nonprofit leadership, grant management and more, bringing advanced analytical and leadership skills that are highly valued across sectors.\nBenefits of a doctoral degree include specialized expertise, professional credibility, expanded career opportunities, maximized earning potential and leadership development.\nReady to find your program? Browse the full list of NIU doctoral degrees.\nExplore Doctoral Programs\nAcademic Programs\nAcademics Overview\nMaster's Degree Programs\nAccelerated Master's Degree Programs\nSpecialist Degree Programs\nDoctoral Degree Programs\nCertificates of Graduate Study\nNon-degree Study\nColleges\nOnline Programs\nLaw\nContact Us\nThe Graduate School\nWilliston Hall 100\n815-753-0395\ngradsch@niu.edu\nNorthern Illinois University\n1425 West Lincoln Hwy\nDeKalb, IL 60115\nDirections and Maps\nOffice Hours\nMonday | 8 a.m. to 4:30 p.m. (virtual, by appoin